Chimera: no launcher, and a game that cannot run says why.

A Chimera machine plays the one game its project gives. When ScummVM would
show its launcher (no game was found, or the player asked to return to it)
or its error box (the engine could not start), it calls the core instead,
which ends the machine with ScummVM's reason. Only with CHIMERA_BACKEND
defined (the core defines it for base/main.cpp alone); upstream's builds
are unchanged.

--- a/base/main.cpp
+++ b/base/main.cpp
@@ -100,7 +100,18 @@
 
